const e="kempsey-eisteddfod",m=2025,o="Read the whole 2025 VISD syllabus. It prints no venue name or address, no event dates, no contact person or phone number, no points or judging criteria and no ranks. Those sections are empty. The older speech and dance pages on the organiser's previous site are not reachable and were not used. Set piece texts are named but not copied. The syllabus is a past edition: closing date, fees and prizes are kept as variables.",t=JSON.parse(`{"Title":"Rules and Syllabus Conditions","Subtitle":"Kempsey Eisteddfod vocal, instrumental, speech and drama: rules, entry and awards","NoticeTitle":"Please Read Before Registering","Notice":"All entries are online at {{EntryWebsite}} and this is the only way to enter. Entries close {{EntriesClose}}. Late entries are not accepted. Check your entries carefully.","Notes":["Entrants must enter the school stage they are in for the year of the eisteddfod.","Public notice of programme changes is given at least 14 days before the eisteddfod on Facebook and on the official website. Checking for changes is the responsibility of competitors, parents and teachers."],"Sections":[{"Key":"general","Title":"General rules","Items":["In these rules 'Committee' means the Vocal and Instrumental Committee of the Kempsey Eisteddfod Society Inc. (rule 1).","Competitors, teachers and parents must know all the rules. Not knowing a rule is not accepted as a reason for breaking it. All entrants are taken to agree to the rules (rule 2).","The Committee may amend or refuse any entry; divide sections with 12 or more entries; amend the programme at any time; reduce or change the published prizes; cancel or combine events with too few entries; and appoint a new adjudicator (rule 4).","First, second and third prizes are awarded whatever the number of competitors (rule 7).","Do not ask to change the dates or times of competitions. After the official programme is printed no changes to times are allowed. Special requests must be sent in writing at the time of entry, with no guarantee that they can be met (rule 14).","If a competitor is entered in the wrong section by error, the Committee may move the entry to the correct section (rule 15).","All competitors take part at their own risk (rule 30).","Photography: by taking part, a competitor agrees that the Kempsey Eisteddfod Society may use and publish photographs or videos taken during any of its events. Images are not identified by full name or personal details without approval from the person, parent or guardian. A person who does not agree must tell the President in writing before the event starts. The Society decides who may take photos or videos at its premises or events."]},{"Key":"eligibility","Title":"Who may enter","Items":["School stages: Early Stage 1 is Kindergarten or Pre School; Stage 1 is Years 1 and 2; Stage 2 is Years 3 and 4; Stage 3 is Years 5 and 6; Stage 4 is Years 7 and 8; Stage 5 is Years 9 and 10; Stage 6 is Years 11 and 12. Open Age is competitors over 18 years.","Entrants must enter the school stage they are in for the year of the eisteddfod.","Competitors must compete in their own school stage sections and not outside their own age group, unless a section is shown in the schedule as open to all ages (rule 8).","Entries in an Open solo section are accepted only from competitors aged 18 years and over, unless stated otherwise. In Open duet and trio sections one competitor must be over 18 (rule 10).","A competitor must not perform the same item in more than one section of the current eisteddfod (rule 11).","A competitor must not enter any section twice, especially in groups (rule 12).","In duets and trios, competitors enter in the stage section of the oldest competitor (instrumental duet and trio sections).","Novice sections: the player must have had tuition for less than two years.","Graded Pianoforte Solo: for performers who have learned or are learning examination pieces for AMEB Piano, AMEB Piano for Leisure, Trinity, Suzuki, Yamaha or similar grade systems. There are no age restrictions.","Small Schools Choir and Small Schools Band: for schools with an enrolment under 50 students.","Own Composition: the composer must perform. The composition may be a joint work, but every composer and lyricist must be named, and a written or computer score must be handed in.","Championships: competitors must compete in at least 2 other sections to be eligible, and the championship pieces must not have been performed before at the eisteddfod by the competitor (rule 9).","Junior Championships are for Stages 1, 2 and 3. Senior/Open Championships are for Stages 4, 5 and 6 (rule 9)."]},{"Key":"registration","Title":"How to enter","Items":["All entries are placed online at {{EntryWebsite}}. This is the only form of entry.","Entries close {{EntriesClose}}. Late entries are not accepted.","All details must be completed on the online form, except the date of birth for Open competitors.","No entry is accepted unless it comes with the full fees.","Check your entries carefully before you send them.","Make your own arrangements with your accompanist as soon as you receive the programme.","A photocopy of each own choice piece, with the section and competitor number clearly marked in the top left corner, must be handed in for the adjudicator at least 3 sections before the performance. The competitor must follow copyright law. All photocopies are destroyed at the end of the competition (rule 25).","Music accompaniment goes on a memory stick, one track per stick, clearly labelled, and is given to the Office before the performance. Where the syllabus says so, speech and drama own choice copies are also handed to the Office before the performance.","On arrival, competitors must report to the Eisteddfod Office (rule 13)."]},{"Key":"fees","Title":"Entry fees","Items":["Entry fees: {{EntryFees}}.","No entries are accepted without full fees.","All children under 16 must be accompanied by a supervising adult in the eisteddfod hall, and accompanying adults pay the session admission fee. Teachers with school groups and accompanists are exempt. Competitors enter free for the session of their performance only (rules 21 and 22)."]},{"Key":"dates","Title":"Dates","Items":["Entries close {{EntriesClose}}.","Public notice of programme changes is given at least 14 days before the eisteddfod begins."]},{"Key":"judging","Title":"Judging and results","Items":["The adjudicator's decision is final (rule 5).","The adjudicator may reduce or withdraw prizes if a satisfactory standard is not reached; may, with Committee approval, increase the number of prizes in a section; and may stop a performance at any time. Stopping a performance does not necessarily mean disqualification or disapproval (rule 5).","Time limits are strictly observed (rule 5).","Marks may be given for quality of choice and for stage presentation. Dress and presentation are part of the performance and may be taken into account (rule 26).","Competitors in championships are judged as suitable for their stage or age."]},{"Key":"complaints","Title":"Protests","Items":["A protest arising out of, or not covered by, these rules must be given to the Committee in writing straight after the session in which the protest arose. It must come with a deposit of {{ProtestDeposit}}, which is lost if the protest is found to be unfounded (rule 3)."]},{"Key":"conduct","Title":"Conduct and staging","Items":["Competitors must be on time for their sections and compete in the order in the official programme unless the organising committee says otherwise. A competitor who is not present when called may be disqualified (rule 13).","Competitors, teachers and parents must not approach the adjudicator during sessions. Breaking this rule may lead to disqualification (rule 16).","No prompting by teachers or parents is allowed, except by the adjudicator (rule 17).","Photography, recording or video equipment may not be used during any section without the permission of the Kempsey Eisteddfod Society, in line with Australian copyright and privacy law (rule 18).","Performances must be suitable for all audience ages and respectful to the venue. Offensive or blasphemous language and some adult themes are not accepted; the item is stopped and the competitor disqualified (rule 19).","No rehearsals or practice on stage once the eisteddfod has started. Brief sound checks are allowed (rule 20).","The accompanying teacher is responsible for pupils' behaviour while they wait to perform. Competitors must wait their turn quietly and with respect for other performers (rule 23).","Originals must be used in performance, except for copies made to help turn pages. Authorised internet purchases are allowed (rule 24).","Accompaniment is allowed only in sections where the syllabus says so. Music is on a memory stick, one track per stick. Supporting vocals are not allowed in vocal sections. Backing music with small fragments of added harmony is accepted. Lead cues may be used for Stage 3 and under in instrumental sections only. All other sections need live accompaniment, which means piano unless stated (rule 27).","All pieces performed should be chosen from the classical repertoire unless stated otherwise. The quality and suitability of the selection is taken into account (rule 28).","A piano is provided (rule 29)."]},{"Key":"teams","Title":"Groups, choirs and bands","Items":["Small vocal groups: one song, minimum 6 voices, maximum 8 minutes, costumes encouraged.","Choirs: two contrasting songs, own choice, minimum 10 voices, maximum 8 minutes.","Ensembles: one song, 4 to 6 players.","Bands may include school, rock and jazz bands and may include vocalists. Teachers may conduct and play simple accompaniment, but are not adjudicated. All other competitors must be within the age limit of the section.","School Choral Speaking Group: two pieces from memory, maximum 30 voices, no props.","Short play: minimum 3 people from memory, overall time 15 minutes including stage preparation and clearing, with minimum props.","Impromptu Play: minimum 3 and maximum 8 performers. No competitor may appear in more than one play.","Shakespearean Play: own choice, from memory, minimum 3 people, minimum props. No competitor may appear in more than one play per section.","Debating: 3 members in each team. Where a school enters two teams, a student must not appear in both."]},{"Key":"points","Title":"Championships","Items":["Championships are awarded in vocal, instrumental, pianoforte and speech. See each championship competition for its time and programme.","Instrumental and Pianoforte Championships are awarded only if three or more competitors compete, or at the adjudicator's discretion."]},{"Key":"prizes","Title":"Awards","Items":["Stages Early Stage 1 to 3: first place receives a medal; second, third, highly commended and encouragement receive a ribbon.","Stages 4 to 6: first place receives a monetary prize; second, third, highly commended and encouragement receive a ribbon.","All competitors receive a ribbon.","Championship awards ({{ChampionshipPrize}} each): Junior Piano Championship, Senior Piano Championship, Amanda Harvey Junior Vocal Championship, Senior Vocal Championship, Regional Finance Solutions Instrumental Championship, Leonie Capararo Senior Instrumental Championship, Junior Speech Championship (Stages 1 and 2) and Senior Speech Championship (Stages 4, 5, 6 and Open age).","Special awards ({{SpecialAwardPrize}} each) are named for sponsors and given for: Most Promising Instrumentalist (Stage 3 and under; Stage 4 to 6 and Open), Most Promising Pianist (Stage 3 and under; Stage 4 to 6 and Open), Most Outstanding Local Instrumentalist (all stages), Most Promising Local Guitarist (all stages), Most Promising Vocalist (Stage 3 and under; Stage 4 to 6), Most Outstanding Local Vocalist (all stages), Most Promising Speech Competitor (Stage 3 and under; Stage 4 to 6), Most Successful Speech Competitor (on the adjudicator's marks), Most Promising Drama Competitor (Stage 3 and under; Stage 4 to 6) and Most Successful Drama Competitor (on the adjudicator's marks).","The awards list is as at the time of printing. Sponsors are added as they come in."]},{"Key":"other","Title":"Other parts of the eisteddfod","Items":["This template covers the vocal, instrumental, speech and drama syllabus. Dance sections are in a separate syllabus and are not built here."]}],"Documents":[{"Title":"VISD Syllabus 2025 (PDF)","Url":"https://kempseyeisteddfod.squarespace.com/s/VISD-Syllabus-2025-Final-update-144.pdf"}]}`),n=[],a=[],i=JSON.parse(`[{"Title":"Vocal Solo - Own Choice","Source":"VISD Syllabus 2025, Vocal Solos","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["4 minutes."],"Rules":["One song, own choice, any theme (sections M001 to M048). Accompaniment is allowed on a labelled memory stick, one track per stick, given to the Office before the performance."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- 4 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- One song, own choice, any theme (sections M001 to M048). Accompaniment is allowed on a labelled memory stick, one track per stick, given to the Office before the performance."},{"Title":"Vocal Solo - Hymn","Source":"VISD Syllabus 2025, Vocal Solos","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["4 minutes."],"Rules":["One song, own choice, any theme (sections M001 to M048). Accompaniment is allowed on a labelled memory stick, one track per stick, given to the Office before the performance."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- 4 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- One song, own choice, any theme (sections M001 to M048). Accompaniment is allowed on a labelled memory stick, one track per stick, given to the Office before the performance."},{"Title":"Vocal Solo - Theme from Musical Theatre, Film or TV","Source":"VISD Syllabus 2025, Vocal Solos","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["4 minutes."],"Rules":["One song, own choice, any theme (sections M001 to M048). Accompaniment is allowed on a labelled memory stick, one track per stick, given to the Office before the performance."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- 4 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- One song, own choice, any theme (sections M001 to M048). Accompaniment is allowed on a labelled memory stick, one track per stick, given to the Office before the performance."},{"Title":"Vocal Solo - Popular Song","Source":"VISD Syllabus 2025, Vocal Solos","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["4 minutes."],"Rules":["One song, own choice, any theme (sections M001 to M048). Accompaniment is allowed on a labelled memory stick, one track per stick, given to the Office before the performance."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- 4 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- One song, own choice, any theme (sections M001 to M048). Accompaniment is allowed on a labelled memory stick, one track per stick, given to the Office before the performance."},{"Title":"Vocal Solo - Nursery Rhyme in Costume","Source":"VISD Syllabus 2025, Vocal Solos","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["4 minutes."],"Rules":["One song, own choice, any theme (sections M001 to M048). Accompaniment is allowed on a labelled memory stick, one track per stick, given to the Office before the performance."],"Allowed":["Costume."],"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- 4 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- One song, own choice, any theme (sections M001 to M048). Accompaniment is allowed on a labelled memory stick, one track per stick, given to the Office before the performance.\\n\\n## Allowed\\n- Costume."},{"Title":"Vocal Solo - Song in Costume","Source":"VISD Syllabus 2025, Vocal Solos","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["4 minutes."],"Rules":["One song, own choice, any theme (sections M001 to M048). Accompaniment is allowed on a labelled memory stick, one track per stick, given to the Office before the performance."],"Allowed":["Movement and dance are permitted. Costume."],"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- 4 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- One song, own choice, any theme (sections M001 to M048). Accompaniment is allowed on a labelled memory stick, one track per stick, given to the Office before the performance.\\n\\n## Allowed\\n- Movement and dance are permitted. Costume."},{"Title":"Vocalist and Accompanist","Source":"VISD Syllabus 2025, Vocal and Accompanist (M030 to M033)","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["5 minutes."],"Rules":["The accompaniment may be on any instrument. Both competitors are judged."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- 5 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- The accompaniment may be on any instrument. Both competitors are judged."},{"Title":"Vocal Self Accompanied","Source":"VISD Syllabus 2025, Vocal Self Accompanied (M034 to M037)","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["The vocalist accompanies themselves."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Rules\\n- The vocalist accompanies themselves."},{"Title":"Vocal Duet, Trio or Quartet","Source":"VISD Syllabus 2025, Vocal Duets, Trio or Quartet (M038 to M041)","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["Stages 5 and 6 (M040) and Stage 6 and Open (M041) overlap at Stage 6 by design."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Rules\\n- Stages 5 and 6 (M040) and Stage 6 and Open (M041) overlap at Stage 6 by design."},{"Title":"Light Entertainment Vocal Group","Source":"VISD Syllabus 2025, Small Vocal Groups (M042 to M045)","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Maximum 8 minutes."],"Rules":["One song, minimum 6 voices.","Accompaniment allowed on a labelled memory stick, one track per stick, given to the Office before the performance."],"Allowed":["Costumes are encouraged."],"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Maximum 8 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- One song, minimum 6 voices.\\n- Accompaniment allowed on a labelled memory stick, one track per stick, given to the Office before the performance.\\n\\n## Allowed\\n- Costumes are encouraged."},{"Title":"Choir","Source":"VISD Syllabus 2025, Choirs (M046 to M050)","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Maximum 8 minutes."],"Rules":["Two contrasting songs, own choice, minimum 10 voices.","Accompaniment allowed on a labelled memory stick, one track per stick.","Small Schools Choir is for schools with an enrolment under 50 students."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Maximum 8 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Two contrasting songs, own choice, minimum 10 voices.\\n- Accompaniment allowed on a labelled memory stick, one track per stick.\\n- Small Schools Choir is for schools with an enrolment under 50 students."},{"Title":"All Ability Choir","Source":"VISD Syllabus 2025, Choirs (M051)","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["Own song choice.","Helpers may assist. Backing music is given on a memory stick, one track per stick, to the Office before the performance."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Rules\\n- Own song choice.\\n- Helpers may assist. Backing music is given on a memory stick, one track per stick, to the Office before the performance."},{"Title":"Aged Care Choir","Source":"VISD Syllabus 2025, Choirs (M052)","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["Own song choice.","Helpers may assist. Backing music is given on a labelled memory stick, one track per stick, to the Office before the performance."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Rules\\n- Own song choice.\\n- Helpers may assist. Backing music is given on a labelled memory stick, one track per stick, to the Office before the performance."},{"Title":"Group Action Song in Costume","Source":"VISD Syllabus 2025, Group Action Song in Costume (M184 to M187)","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["5 minutes."],"Rules":["One song. Music accompaniment is allowed, loaded on a memory stick, one track per stick."],"Allowed":["Costume. The Early Stage 1 section is a song in costume."],"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- 5 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- One song. Music accompaniment is allowed, loaded on a memory stick, one track per stick.\\n\\n## Allowed\\n- Costume. The Early Stage 1 section is a song in costume."},{"Title":"Vocal Championship","Source":"VISD Syllabus 2025, Vocal Championships (M053, M054)","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Junior Vocal Championship (Stages 1 to 3): 6 minutes. Senior Vocal Championship: 10 minutes."],"Rules":["Competitors must compete in at least 2 other sections on their chosen song.","The programme is 2 contrasting own choice songs.","Time limits must be followed. Failing to do so may lead to disqualification.","The Senior section is printed as Stage 5 and 6, while the general rule gives Senior/Open Championships as Stages 4, 5 and 6."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Competitors are judged as suitable for their stage or age."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Junior Vocal Championship (Stages 1 to 3): 6 minutes. Senior Vocal Championship: 10 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Competitors must compete in at least 2 other sections on their chosen song.\\n- The programme is 2 contrasting own choice songs.\\n- Time limits must be followed. Failing to do so may lead to disqualification.\\n- The Senior section is printed as Stage 5 and 6, while the general rule gives Senior/Open Championships as Stages 4, 5 and 6.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Competitors are judged as suitable for their stage or age."},{"Title":"Pianoforte - HSC Music Programme Work","Source":"VISD Syllabus 2025, Pianoforte Sections (M102, M114, M128)","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["5 minutes."],"Rules":null,"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- 5 minutes."},{"Title":"Instrumental Duet or Trio","Source":"VISD Syllabus 2025, Instrumental Duet, Trio (M138 to M143)","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["Any combination of instruments. Competitors enter in the stage section of the oldest competitor.","May include piano accompaniment that is not adjudicated."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Rules\\n- Any combination of instruments. Competitors enter in the stage section of the oldest competitor.\\n- May include piano accompaniment that is not adjudicated."},{"Title":"Novice Instrumental Solo","Source":"VISD Syllabus 2025, Novice Instrumental (M144 to M149)","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["The instrumentalist must have had tuition for less than two years."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Rules\\n- The instrumentalist must have had tuition for less than two years."},{"Title":"Novice Pianist","Source":"VISD Syllabus 2025, Novice Pianist (M150 to M155)","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["The pianist must have had tuition for less than two years."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Rules\\n- The pianist must have had tuition for less than two years."},{"Title":"Graded Pianoforte Solo","Source":"VISD Syllabus 2025, Graded Piano Solo (M156 to M161)","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["For performers who have learned or are learning examination pieces for AMEB Piano, AMEB Piano for Leisure, Trinity, Suzuki, Yamaha or similar grade systems. No age restrictions.","Time limits: Preliminary and Grade 1: 2 minutes; Grades 2 and 3: 3 minutes; Grades 4 and 5: 4 minutes."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Rules\\n- For performers who have learned or are learning examination pieces for AMEB Piano, AMEB Piano for Leisure, Trinity, Suzuki, Yamaha or similar grade systems. No age restrictions.\\n- Time limits: Preliminary and Grade 1: 2 minutes; Grades 2 and 3: 3 minutes; Grades 4 and 5: 4 minutes."},{"Title":"Nuvo Instrumental Group","Source":"VISD Syllabus 2025, Nuvo Instrumental Groups (M167 to M170)","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["Any combination of Nuvo instruments. May include vocalists.","Teachers may conduct and play simple accompaniment, but are not adjudicated."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Rules\\n- Any combination of Nuvo instruments. May include vocalists.\\n- Teachers may conduct and play simple accompaniment, but are not adjudicated."},{"Title":"Instrumental Ensemble","Source":"VISD Syllabus 2025, Ensembles (M188 to M191)","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["One song, minimum 4 and maximum 6 players."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Rules\\n- One song, minimum 4 and maximum 6 players."},{"Title":"Band","Source":"VISD Syllabus 2025, Band Sections (M173 to M176)","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Two pieces, 10 minutes."],"Rules":["May include school, rock and jazz bands, and may include vocalists.","Teachers may conduct and play simple accompaniment, but are not adjudicated. All other competitors must be within the age limit of the section.","Small Schools Band: schools with an enrolment under 50, minimum 5 players. Primary Band (Stages 1 to 3) and Secondary Band (Stages 4 to 6): minimum 5 players. Small Band (Open age): minimum 5 players."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Two pieces, 10 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- May include school, rock and jazz bands, and may include vocalists.\\n- Teachers may conduct and play simple accompaniment, but are not adjudicated. All other competitors must be within the age limit of the section.\\n- Small Schools Band: schools with an enrolment under 50, minimum 5 players. Primary Band (Stages 1 to 3) and Secondary Band (Stages 4 to 6): minimum 5 players. Small Band (Open age): minimum 5 players."},{"Title":"Large Open Band","Source":"VISD Syllabus 2025, Band Sections (M177)","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Two pieces, 10 minutes."],"Rules":["Open age. Minimum 15 players."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Two pieces, 10 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Open age. Minimum 15 players."},{"Title":"All Ability Band","Source":"VISD Syllabus 2025, Band Sections (M178)","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Two pieces, 10 minutes."],"Rules":["Open age, own song choice.","Helpers may assist. Costumes are allowed. Backing music is given on a memory stick, one track per stick, to the Office before the performance."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Two pieces, 10 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Open age, own song choice.\\n- Helpers may assist. Costumes are allowed. Backing music is given on a memory stick, one track per stick, to the Office before the performance."},{"Title":"Own Composition","Source":"VISD Syllabus 2025, Own Composition (M179)","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["5 minutes."],"Rules":["The composition may be a joint work, but all composers and lyricists must be named.","A written or computer-made score must be handed in.","The composer must perform."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- 5 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- The composition may be a joint work, but all composers and lyricists must be named.\\n- A written or computer-made score must be handed in.\\n- The composer must perform."},{"Title":"Instrumental Championship","Source":"VISD Syllabus 2025, Instrumental Championships (M180, M181)","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Junior (Stages 1 to 3): 6 minutes. Senior (Stages 4 to 6): 10 minutes."],"Rules":["Competitors must compete in at least 2 other sections on their chosen instrument. Time limits must be followed; failing to do so may lead to disqualification.","The programme is 2 contrasting pieces of different genre and period, own choice, but not popular, theme or jazz.","Championships are awarded only if three or more competitors compete, or at the adjudicator's discretion.","Both pieces must be played on the same instrument. The repertoire must show knowledge of the genre. Credit is given for music choice and for suitability to the age. Not meeting these rules leads to disqualification."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Competitors are judged as suitable for their stage or age."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Junior (Stages 1 to 3): 6 minutes. Senior (Stages 4 to 6): 10 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Competitors must compete in at least 2 other sections on their chosen instrument. Time limits must be followed; failing to do so may lead to disqualification.\\n- The programme is 2 contrasting pieces of different genre and period, own choice, but not popular, theme or jazz.\\n- Championships are awarded only if three or more competitors compete, or at the adjudicator's discretion.\\n- Both pieces must be played on the same instrument. The repertoire must show knowledge of the genre. Credit is given for music choice and for suitability to the age. Not meeting these rules leads to disqualification.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Competitors are judged as suitable for their stage or age."},{"Title":"Pianoforte Championship","Source":"VISD Syllabus 2025, Pianoforte Championships (M182, M183)","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Junior (Stages 1 to 3): 6 minutes. Senior (Stages 4 to 6): 10 minutes."],"Rules":["Competitors must compete in at least 2 other sections on their chosen instrument. Time limits must be followed; failing to do so may lead to disqualification.","The programme is 2 contrasting pieces of different genre and period, own choice, but not popular, theme or jazz.","Championships are awarded only if three or more competitors compete, or at the adjudicator's discretion.","Both pieces must be played on the same instrument. The repertoire must show knowledge of the genre. Credit is given for music choice and for suitability to the age. Not meeting these rules leads to disqualification."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Competitors are judged as suitable for their stage or age."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Junior (Stages 1 to 3): 6 minutes. Senior (Stages 4 to 6): 10 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Competitors must compete in at least 2 other sections on their chosen instrument. Time limits must be followed; failing to do so may lead to disqualification.\\n- The programme is 2 contrasting pieces of different genre and period, own choice, but not popular, theme or jazz.\\n- Championships are awarded only if three or more competitors compete, or at the adjudicator's discretion.\\n- Both pieces must be played on the same instrument. The repertoire must show knowledge of the genre. Credit is given for music choice and for suitability to the age. Not meeting these rules leads to disqualification.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Competitors are judged as suitable for their stage or age."},{"Title":"Verse or Nursery Rhyme in Costume","Source":"VISD Syllabus 2025, Early Stage 1 (S001)","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["3 minutes."],"Rules":["Own choice, from memory, in costume."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- 3 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Own choice, from memory, in costume."},{"Title":"Set Verse","Source":"VISD Syllabus 2025, Set Pieces","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["3 minutes."],"Rules":["From memory. Set verses: Early Stage 1 'Little Wind' by Kate Greenaway; Stage 1 'A Baby Sardine' by Spike Milligan; Stage 2 'I Wish I Were a Superhero' by James McDonald; Stage 3 'Sunning' by James S. Tippett; Stage 4 'The Arrow and the Song' by Henry Wadsworth Longfellow. The texts are printed at the end of the syllabus."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- 3 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- From memory. Set verses: Early Stage 1 'Little Wind' by Kate Greenaway; Stage 1 'A Baby Sardine' by Spike Milligan; Stage 2 'I Wish I Were a Superhero' by James McDonald; Stage 3 'Sunning' by James S. Tippett; Stage 4 'The Arrow and the Song' by Henry Wadsworth Longfellow. The texts are printed at the end of the syllabus."},{"Title":"Poem - Own Choice","Source":"VISD Syllabus 2025, Speech and Drama Syllabus","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["3 minutes."],"Rules":["Own choice, from memory. Verse can be in any style (Australian, lyrical, light and so on)."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- 3 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Own choice, from memory. Verse can be in any style (Australian, lyrical, light and so on)."},{"Title":"Humorous or Satiric Verse","Source":"VISD Syllabus 2025, Speech and Drama Syllabus","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["3 minutes."],"Rules":["Own choice, from memory."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- 3 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Own choice, from memory."},{"Title":"Solo Verse in Costume","Source":"VISD Syllabus 2025, Speech and Drama Syllabus","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["3 minutes."],"Rules":["Own choice, from memory. Costume is optional for Stages 5, 6 and Open."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- 3 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Own choice, from memory. Costume is optional for Stages 5, 6 and Open."},{"Title":"Australian Bush Poem","Source":"VISD Syllabus 2025, Speech and Drama Syllabus","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["3 minutes."],"Rules":["Own choice, from memory.","The poem must have Australian content and be written by an Australian poet."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- 3 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Own choice, from memory.\\n- The poem must have Australian content and be written by an Australian poet."},{"Title":"Prose Reading - Set Piece","Source":"VISD Syllabus 2025, Set Pieces","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["3 minutes."],"Rules":["The reader must read from the paper, not recite from memory. Set pieces: Early Stage 1 'Zac the Rat' by Starfall; Stage 1 'One Little Dinosaur' by Pip Williams and Richard Watson; Stage 2 'The Twits' by Roald Dahl; Stage 3 'Unreal' by Paul Jennings; Stage 4 'Demon Dentist' by David Williams.","Prose is made up of sentences and paragraphs without metre or rhyme. Performers must read straight from the text on stage."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- 3 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- The reader must read from the paper, not recite from memory. Set pieces: Early Stage 1 'Zac the Rat' by Starfall; Stage 1 'One Little Dinosaur' by Pip Williams and Richard Watson; Stage 2 'The Twits' by Roald Dahl; Stage 3 'Unreal' by Paul Jennings; Stage 4 'Demon Dentist' by David Williams.\\n- Prose is made up of sentences and paragraphs without metre or rhyme. Performers must read straight from the text on stage."},{"Title":"Bible Reading - Set Piece","Source":"VISD Syllabus 2025, Set Pieces","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["3 minutes."],"Rules":["Read from the paper, not recited from memory. Set pieces: Stage 2 Psalm 23:1 to 3; Stage 3 Timothy 4:11 to 16; Stage 4 Luke 9:12 to 17; Stages 5, 6 and Open Genesis 1:1 to 18."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- 3 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Read from the paper, not recited from memory. Set pieces: Stage 2 Psalm 23:1 to 3; Stage 3 Timothy 4:11 to 16; Stage 4 Luke 9:12 to 17; Stages 5, 6 and Open Genesis 1:1 to 18."},{"Title":"Public Speaking - Own Topic","Source":"VISD Syllabus 2025, Speech and Drama Syllabus","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["5 minutes."],"Rules":["A speech on a topic, written and spoken by the competitor. Prompt cards are allowed."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- 5 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- A speech on a topic, written and spoken by the competitor. Prompt cards are allowed."},{"Title":"Mime - Set Topic","Source":"VISD Syllabus 2025, Speech and Drama Syllabus","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["3 minutes."],"Rules":["Black clothing. Set topics: Stage 1 'Catching Butterflies'; Stage 2 'Washing the Dog'; Stage 3 'Setting up a Birthday Party'; Stage 4 'Learning to Drive a Car'; Stages 5, 6 and Open 'Buying Groceries'.","Mime uses exaggerated facial expressions and body movements, instead of words, to tell the audience what is happening."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- 3 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Black clothing. Set topics: Stage 1 'Catching Butterflies'; Stage 2 'Washing the Dog'; Stage 3 'Setting up a Birthday Party'; Stage 4 'Learning to Drive a Car'; Stages 5, 6 and Open 'Buying Groceries'.\\n- Mime uses exaggerated facial expressions and body movements, instead of words, to tell the audience what is happening."},{"Title":"Write and Read Your Own Composition","Source":"VISD Syllabus 2025, Speech and Drama Syllabus","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["3 minutes."],"Rules":["The entrant writes the composition without help and reads it on stage.","It is judged on the written content and on the reading."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- 3 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- The entrant writes the composition without help and reads it on stage.\\n- It is judged on the written content and on the reading."},{"Title":"Monologue","Source":"VISD Syllabus 2025, Stage 3 (S028)","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["5 minutes."],"Rules":["An extract from a play or poem. Costume and props are optional.","A monologue is a speech by one person, or a long one-sided conversation."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- 5 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- An extract from a play or poem. Costume and props are optional.\\n- A monologue is a speech by one person, or a long one-sided conversation."},{"Title":"Duologue","Source":"VISD Syllabus 2025, Stage 3 (S027)","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["5 minutes."],"Rules":["An extract from a play or poem. Costume and props are optional.","A duologue is dramatic speech between two people."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- 5 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- An extract from a play or poem. Costume and props are optional.\\n- A duologue is dramatic speech between two people."},{"Title":"HSC Monologue","Source":"VISD Syllabus 2025, Stages 5, 6 and Open (S050)","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["11 minutes."],"Rules":["Own choice."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- 11 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Own choice."},{"Title":"Shakespearean Monologue","Source":"VISD Syllabus 2025, Stages 5, 6 and Open (S051)","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["5 minutes."],"Rules":["Costume is optional."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- 5 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Costume is optional."},{"Title":"Shakespearean Duologue","Source":"VISD Syllabus 2025, Stages 5, 6 and Open (S052)","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["5 minutes."],"Rules":["Costume is optional."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- 5 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Costume is optional."},{"Title":"Recital for Two","Source":"VISD Syllabus 2025, Recital for Two (S053 to S057)","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Maximum 3 minutes; Stage 4: maximum 5 minutes."],"Rules":["Poem or reading, own choice, read or memorised.","It must include separate readings by each member and at least 25% narration together.","Minimal movement and gesture on the spot are allowed. No props. Performers may choose their own scripts. Each performer should hold a copy of the script.","Minimal face paint, ears and whiskers are acceptable where age and script suit."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Maximum 3 minutes; Stage 4: maximum 5 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Poem or reading, own choice, read or memorised.\\n- It must include separate readings by each member and at least 25% narration together.\\n- Minimal movement and gesture on the spot are allowed. No props. Performers may choose their own scripts. Each performer should hold a copy of the script.\\n- Minimal face paint, ears and whiskers are acceptable where age and script suit."},{"Title":"Poem for Two","Source":"VISD Syllabus 2025, Poem for Two (S070 to S074)","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Maximum 3 minutes; Stage 4: maximum 5 minutes."],"Rules":["Poem or reading, own choice. The two must read together.","Both competitors must be from the same school stage."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Maximum 3 minutes; Stage 4: maximum 5 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Poem or reading, own choice. The two must read together.\\n- Both competitors must be from the same school stage."},{"Title":"Short Play or Excerpt","Source":"VISD Syllabus 2025, Short Play or Excerpt from Play, Poetry or Prose (S058, S059)","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Maximum 15 minutes in total, including stage preparation and clearing."],"Rules":["Minimum 3 people, from memory. Props kept to a minimum."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Maximum 15 minutes in total, including stage preparation and clearing.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Minimum 3 people, from memory. Props kept to a minimum."},{"Title":"Impromptu Play","Source":"VISD Syllabus 2025, Impromptu Play (S060, S061)","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Maximum 3 minutes."],"Rules":["Minimum 3 and maximum 8 performers. No competitor may appear in more than one play.","The adjudicator sets the subject and gives it to the performers before they perform."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Maximum 3 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Minimum 3 and maximum 8 performers. No competitor may appear in more than one play.\\n- The adjudicator sets the subject and gives it to the performers before they perform."},{"Title":"Shakespearean Play","Source":"VISD Syllabus 2025, Shakespearean Play (S062)","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["Own choice, from memory, minimum 3 people. Props kept to a minimum. No competitor may appear in more than one play per section."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Rules\\n- Own choice, from memory, minimum 3 people. Props kept to a minimum. No competitor may appear in more than one play per section."},{"Title":"School Choral Speaking Group","Source":"VISD Syllabus 2025, School Choral Speaking Group (S063 to S066)","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["Two pieces from memory: the set piece and an own choice piece. No props. Maximum 30 voices.","Set pieces: Early Stage 1 'Cos I'm the Youngest' by Lee-Ann Holmes; Stage 1 'Bugs' by Andrew Chant; Stage 2 'The Macleay' by Alison Davis; Stage 3 'The Ant Explorer' by C.J. Dennis."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Rules\\n- Two pieces from memory: the set piece and an own choice piece. No props. Maximum 30 voices.\\n- Set pieces: Early Stage 1 'Cos I'm the Youngest' by Lee-Ann Holmes; Stage 1 'Bugs' by Andrew Chant; Stage 2 'The Macleay' by Alison Davis; Stage 3 'The Ant Explorer' by C.J. Dennis."},{"Title":"Debating","Source":"VISD Syllabus 2025, Debating (S067)","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Each speaker has 4 minutes in the rules (a warning bell at 3 minutes and a continuous bell at 4 minutes); the section is printed as '3 minutes per speaker'. Teams have 30 minutes to prepare."],"Rules":["The chairperson is a member of the Eisteddfod Committee.","Each team has three members. Where a school enters two teams, a student must not be in both.","A coin toss decides the sides: heads is Affirmative and tails is Negative.","The topics are given on the day. Each debate uses one of these categories: Youth Issues, Media and Entertainment, Sport, World Affairs. Each debate has a different topic.","Teams may not use mobile electronic devices to prepare or get help from teachers or parents. Once a speaker begins, the team may not help them."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":["Time limits are strictly enforced and penalties apply."]},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Each speaker has 4 minutes in the rules (a warning bell at 3 minutes and a continuous bell at 4 minutes); the section is printed as '3 minutes per speaker'. Teams have 30 minutes to prepare.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- The chairperson is a member of the Eisteddfod Committee.\\n- Each team has three members. Where a school enters two teams, a student must not be in both.\\n- A coin toss decides the sides: heads is Affirmative and tails is Negative.\\n- The topics are given on the day. Each debate uses one of these categories: Youth Issues, Media and Entertainment, Sport, World Affairs. Each debate has a different topic.\\n- Teams may not use mobile electronic devices to prepare or get help from teachers or parents. Once a speaker begins, the team may not help them.\\n\\n## Notes for participants\\n- Time limits are strictly enforced and penalties apply."},{"Title":"Speech Championship","Source":"VISD Syllabus 2025, Speech Championships (S068, S069)","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Maximum 8 minutes."],"Rules":["Two pieces, own choice: a verse (from memory) and a reading not performed before by the competitor at this eisteddfod.","To qualify, competitors must have competed in a verse section and a reading section before the championship."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Competitors are judged as suitable for their stage or age."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Maximum 8 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Two pieces, own choice: a verse (from memory) and a reading not performed before by the competitor at this eisteddfod.\\n- To qualify, competitors must have competed in a verse section and a reading section before the championship.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Competitors are judged as suitable for their stage or age."}]`),s=[],l=[{Key:"EntryWebsite",Kind:"link",Label:"Online entry website",Value:"www.kempseyeisteddfod.org",Source:"VISD Syllabus 2025, page 2"},{Key:"EntriesClose",Kind:"date",Label:"Entries close (midnight)",Value:"2025-04-17",Source:"VISD Syllabus 2025, page 2"},{Key:"EntryFees",Kind:"fee",Label:"Entry fees",Value:"Solos $10.00; Duo, Trio or Quartet $15.00; all groups $20.00; championships $20.00",Source:"VISD Syllabus 2025, page 2"},{Key:"ProtestDeposit",Kind:"fee",Label:"Protest deposit",Value:"$20.00",Source:"VISD Syllabus 2025, rule 3"},{Key:"ChampionshipPrize",Kind:"prize",Label:"Championship prize",Value:"$50",Source:"VISD Syllabus 2025, page 6"},{Key:"SpecialAwardPrize",Kind:"prize",Label:"Special award prize",Value:"$50.00",Source:"VISD Syllabus 2025, page 6"},{Key:"Announcements",Kind:"news",Label:"Notices printed in the syllabus",Value:[{Date:"2025-04-17",Title:"Entries close",Text:"Entries close at midnight on Thursday 17 April 2025. Late entries will not be accepted. Please check your entries carefully.",Url:""},{Date:"",Title:"Programme changes",Text:"Public notice of any changes to the programme will be advertised at least 14 days before the eisteddfod begins on Facebook and on the official website.",Url:""},{Date:"",Title:"Awards",Text:"The awards list is as at the time of printing. Sponsors will be added as they come in.",Url:""}],Source:"VISD Syllabus 2025, pages 2, 3 and 6"}],r=[{Claim:"Rules, fees, closing date, awards, section conditions and set pieces are from the organiser's own 2025 VISD syllabus.",SourceType:"Primary - the event's own rules document",Source:"Kempsey Eisteddfod 2025 VISD Syllabus",Url:"https://kempseyeisteddfod.squarespace.com/s/VISD-Syllabus-2025-Final-update-144.pdf"}],u={TemplateKey:e,Year:2025,Note:o,Page:t,ParticipantTypes:n,AgeGroups:a,Competitions:i,CompetitionAgeGroups:s,Variables:l,Evidence:r};export{a as AgeGroups,s as CompetitionAgeGroups,i as Competitions,r as Evidence,o as Note,t as Page,n as ParticipantTypes,e as TemplateKey,l as Variables,m as Year,u as default};
